      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-05-10T07:32:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is this restricted? Why not let the AP decide it?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 64,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "a44d8ede99936dfe01beeb0f3c3f6d1e5242c3b9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2191439c_ec11a2cd",
        "filename": "common/mkbp_event.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146415
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-05-10T17:46:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The idea here is, the default mask is list of all possible wake sources allowed on a particular device. So you cannot set a new one that is not in the list.  \n\nFor example DRU does not have a keyboard. So keyboard is not set as wake source in the default mask. So setting keyboard as a wake source from kernel should not enable wake from MKBP KEY events.\n\nPlease let me know if this does not make any sense.",
      "parentUuid": "dc79ab13_744dd967",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 64,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "a44d8ede99936dfe01beeb0f3c3f6d1e5242c3b9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4c424e01_7909be80",
        "filename": "include/mkbp_event.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-05-10T07:32:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why? Can you not set it once and use it until AP tells EC not to?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 29,
        "endChar": 76
      },
      "revId": "a44d8ede99936dfe01beeb0f3c3f6d1e5242c3b9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ec71c35_fe4e6676",
        "filename": "include/mkbp_event.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-05-10T07:32:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this should be MKBP events (which is https://cs.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/include/ec_commands.h?q\u003dMKBP_EVENT_+file:%5Esrc/platform/ec/+package:%5Echromeos_public$\u0026g\u003d0\u0026l\u003d3143). Instead it should be host events (which is https://cs.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/include/ec_commands.h?type\u003dcs\u0026q\u003dHOST_EVENT_+file:%5Esrc/platform/ec/+package:%5Echromeos_public$\u0026g\u003d0\u0026l\u003d526)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 29,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "a44d8ede99936dfe01beeb0f3c3f6d1e5242c3b9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0671d237_26e1a29e",
        "filename": "include/mkbp_event.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146415
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-05-10T17:46:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done",
      "parentUuid": "6ec71c35_fe4e6676",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 29,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "a44d8ede99936dfe01beeb0f3c3f6d1e5242c3b9",
